.TH SATSUMA 1 "October 2026" "satsuma 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
satsuma \- zero-click offline file converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B satsuma
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B satsuma \-\-popup
\fIFILE\fR...
.br
.B satsuma \-\-convert
\fIFILE FORMAT\fR
.br
.B satsuma \-\-tool
\fITOOL FILE\fR... [\fIkey=value\fR...]
.br
.B satsuma \-\-list
\fIFILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Satsuma converts images, audio, video, PDFs, documents, slides, spreadsheets, subtitles and
archives locally using ffmpeg, ImageMagick, poppler, pandoc and LibreOffice. Results are written
next to the source file and never overwrite anything.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-popup
Open a borderless wheel at the mouse pointer (used by file manager integrations).
.TP
.BI \-\-wheel " convert|tools|actions"
Wheel to show first.
.TP
.BI \-\-convert " FILE FORMAT"
Convert without a window and print the output path.
.TP
.BI \-\-tool " TOOL FILE..."
Run a file tool, e.g. \fBsatsuma \-\-tool trim clip.mp4 start=0:05 end=0:10\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-list " FILE"
Show the conversions and tools available for a file.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
~/.config/satsuma/config.json, ~/.cache/satsuma/satsuma.log
